! 31edo
!
31edo: 31-tone equal tempered scale consisting of 31 sonically equal divisions per octave. Similar to 1/4-Syntonic Comma meantone, the system was first described by Lemme Rossi in 1666, although Vicentino effectively proposed it in 1555. Step-size is 38.7 cents.
